1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,480
Deserted Island Survival
Days
July 19: Set out
July 20-August 3: Special test
August 4-10: Cruise (free time)
August 11: Return, activity ends
Cards
All students will receive one of the following
eight kinds of cards at random.
Cards can only be traded to students of the same year
in different classes. (No trade-backs allowed)
Basic Cards
Lead-off: Holder may use 50% more points at the start of the test.
Supplement: Doubles private points earned by the holder.
Halve: Halves private point penalties inflicted on the holder.
Bandwagon: Holder designates a group at the start of the test.
Half of private point rewards earned by that group...
Insurance: Gives holder a single day to recover in case of ill health
that would otherwise force a drop-out.
Special Cards
Reinforcement: Holder can exist as the seventh person in a group.
Male/female ratio...
Negate: Holder pays no private points when paying a penalty.
Trial: Holder may increase class points awarded by 50%. However...

3
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:09,570
What makes this different from
last year's version is the scale.

4
00:00:10,330 --> 00:00:12,650
In addition to the testing
period being longer,

5
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:15,480
the island we'll be
using is bigger, as well.

6
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:19,500
And as all class years
will be competing at once,

7
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:22,530
the number of opponents will be
the greatest in school history.

8
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:26,960
I can't reveal all the rules at
this particular moment in time,

9
00:00:27,190 --> 00:00:29,000
but in the upcoming special test,

10
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,880
you'll be able to form large
groups of up to six to cooperate.

11
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:36,390
These large groups will
be based on small groups.

12
00:00:36,390 --> 00:00:40,390
*The class points earned by the top three groups will be
transferred from the years of the bottom three groups.
*Class points will be split equally between classes in the group,
regardless of number of members. (Rounded)
Rules
-Group composition: Groups of up to three people
(*up to four for first-years) must be formed by 7/16.
-Classes and members: Small groups must be of students from the same year,
but not necessarily the same class.
-Male-Female ratio: If a group is mixed-gender,
at least 2/3 of the group must be girls.
-Large group formation: After the special test begins,
large groups of up to six people can be formed.
-Large group conditions: Large groups consisting of four or more
people must contain at least 50% girls.
- Drop-outs and penalties: If all members of a group are unable to continue the test
and drop out, they will fail the test and receive a penalty.

14
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:47,950
Think carefully about what
kind of group you want to form.

15
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:04,380
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

16
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:14,990
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

17
00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:22,740
What did you want to talk
to me about, Koenji?

18
00:02:20,330 --> 00:02:22,750
#6 A Tumultuous Scramble

19
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:27,750
I believe you've neglected
a crucial point, Teacher.

20
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:29,500
A crucial point?

21
00:02:30,110 --> 00:02:32,870
If a student decides to take
the special test alone,

22
00:02:32,870 --> 00:02:35,380
and they're not feeling well that day...

23
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:37,260
What happens then?

24
00:02:37,730 --> 00:02:39,510
A ridiculous question.

25
00:02:40,050 --> 00:02:42,730
Last year, you dropped out due to illness.

26
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:45,640
But this year, there will
be no special treatment.

27
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:49,010
Your penalty will be to
pay six million points.

28
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,270
You don't have enough to pay that.

29
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:56,550
What will you do?
Prioritize your freedom and be expelled?

30
00:02:57,030 --> 00:02:59,900
I suppose we'll find out.

31
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:02,920
You're free to go now, Teacher.

32
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:08,420
By the way...

33
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:12,670
Do you have business with
me, Ayanokoji, my boy?

34
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:18,020
You seem to excel at hiding things.

35
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:23,730
But from you, I cannot ascertain
what is truth and what is lies.

36
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:28,050
I do not trust the words
of a person like that.

37
00:03:28,770 --> 00:03:32,350
You don't seem like the kind
of person to trust anyone.

38
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:34,440
True enough.

39
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:38,360
So, how are you going to
approach the upcoming test?

40
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:40,470
A fine question.

41
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:46,120
There's no harm in asking—
will you allow me to join your group?

42
00:03:46,450 --> 00:03:47,870
I'm afraid not.

43
00:03:48,630 --> 00:03:51,130
There's too much on the
line to involve someone

44
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:53,250
who's sure to drop out on the first day.

45
00:03:54,750 --> 00:03:58,000
I see. I cannot object to that.

46
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,110
Are you sure you can
afford to think that way?

47
00:04:00,110 --> 00:04:04,640
I'll think very carefully about how
to surmount this until the day comes.

48
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:08,640
Deserted Island Survival Test Notes.PDF
Rules
-Group composition: Groups of up to three people
(*up to four for first-years) must be formed by 7/16.
-Classes and members: Small groups must be
of students from the same year,
but not necessarily the same class.
-Male-Female ratio: If a group is mixed-gender,
at least 2/3 of the group must be girls.
-Large group formation:
After the special test begins,
large groups of up to six people can be formed.
-Large group conditions:
Large groups consisting of four or more
people must contain at least 50% girls.
- Drop-outs and penalties: If all members of a group
are unable to continue the test
and drop out, they will
fail the test and receive a penalty.

50
00:04:12,330 --> 00:04:15,100
Forming groups of the most
talented people in the year

51
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:18,370
to aim for the top spots
could mitigate risk,

52
00:04:18,370 --> 00:04:20,710
but it won't change the
class point differentials.

53
00:04:21,090 --> 00:04:24,990
Working within your class is high-risk
but lets you keep all the points,

54
00:04:24,990 --> 00:04:27,070
so it's a chance to make
progress against them.

55
00:04:27,070 --> 00:04:30,620
But what if the other classes
work together without us?

56
00:04:31,370 --> 00:04:35,870
I wonder how Sakayanagi-san, Ryuen-kun,
and Ichinose-san will approach it.

57
00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:38,150
Class A is so far ahead,

58
00:04:38,150 --> 00:04:41,320
all they'll want is to keep
anyone from gaining on them.

59
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:44,260
So what about a three-class alliance?

60
00:04:44,710 --> 00:04:48,720
Classes B through D could work
together to close the gap.

61
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:51,930
The enemy of the enemy
is my friend, you mean?

62
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:53,730
A reasonable idea.

63
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:58,470
But if we propose the idea
of isolating Class A,

64
00:04:58,470 --> 00:05:00,870
Sakayanagi-san will likely retaliate.

65
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:05,340
It would be nice if one of the other
classes would make the offer instead.

66
00:05:10,010 --> 00:05:12,370
It seems they've made their move already.

67
00:05:12,370 --> 00:05:16,340
I've ordered the others not
to form groups just yet.

68
00:05:16,890 --> 00:05:18,880
Have you heard from Ichinose?

69
00:05:19,230 --> 00:05:23,260
I would expect her to propose a
full second-year collaboration.

70
00:05:23,590 --> 00:05:25,390
Not at the moment.

71
00:05:25,390 --> 00:05:28,080
If she wanted all the second-year
students working together,

72
00:05:28,080 --> 00:05:31,760
I would expect her to be
putting feelers out already.

73
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:34,270
In this year's island survival game...

74
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:38,020
Would it be possible to ask
you to take first on your own?

75
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:39,940
Don't be ridiculous.

76
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:44,110
The only thing we know now is that it's
a special test on a deserted island.

77
00:05:44,430 --> 00:05:47,610
I thought you might not even need a group.

78
00:05:48,070 --> 00:05:49,920
If we can take first place,

79
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:52,410
we're guaranteed to gain
on the competition.

80
00:05:52,410 --> 00:05:58,000
Then we can focus on group
formations to prevent expulsion.

81
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:02,510
Students in the bottom five groups will
be penalized with expulsion, after all.

82
00:06:02,870 --> 00:06:06,180
We can't pay the points to save them all.

83
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:07,010
Yes.

84
00:06:07,010 --> 00:06:10,180
We can't make point transfers
once the test has started,

85
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:15,080
so I'd like to get as many points
to the at-risk students as possible,

86
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:17,770
but if the students we lend points
to are hit with the penalty,

87
00:06:17,770 --> 00:06:19,210
the consequences will be terrible.

88
00:06:19,730 --> 00:06:22,650
They'll have to do what they
can to survive on their own.

89
00:06:23,410 --> 00:06:25,570
Can I talk with you again sometime?

90
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:27,660
I'll do what I can.

91
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:29,300
That's all I ask.

92
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:30,280
Thank you.

93
00:06:32,250 --> 00:06:33,130
Hey.

94
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:37,960
Hello there, Ayanokoji-kun!

95
00:06:38,220 --> 00:06:40,440
This is an unusual pairing.

96
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:43,960
I have a bad feeling about this.
Can I just go home?

97
00:06:45,490 --> 00:06:46,960
Ishizaki...

98
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:50,270
You didn't answer our text,
so we came to you.

99
00:06:50,270 --> 00:06:52,470
Can we talk?

100
00:06:53,270 --> 00:06:54,220
You want me...

101
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:55,670
to pair up with you?

102
00:06:55,670 --> 00:06:57,990
Me, Albert, or Shiina...

103
00:06:57,990 --> 00:07:01,850
Just work with someone from Class B!

104
00:07:01,850 --> 00:07:05,460
In other words, you want
me to join Class B?

105
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:06,480
Yeah!

106
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:10,070
Is there some benefit to me in that?

107
00:07:10,070 --> 00:07:12,790
It's not a bad deal for you at all, man.

108
00:07:12,790 --> 00:07:15,000
If we make it to Class A,

109
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:19,710
we'll give you 20 million points
and welcome you into our class.

110
00:07:19,950 --> 00:07:20,720
I want that, too!

111
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:21,710
Yes.

112
00:07:21,710 --> 00:07:24,750
Is Ryuen behind this offer?

113
00:07:25,190 --> 00:07:27,460
Or was this your idea, Ishizaki?

114
00:07:27,690 --> 00:07:29,420
It was my idea!

115
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:31,700
Ryuen-san doesn't know about it.

116
00:07:31,700 --> 00:07:35,050
Have you considered what
will happen if he finds out?

117
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:38,350
Of course not! I can't afford to!

118
00:07:38,350 --> 00:07:40,390
That's part of going for it.

119
00:07:40,390 --> 00:07:45,800
What matters in the special test is to
not lose any second-year class points.

120
00:07:46,250 --> 00:07:50,530
In order to place in the top three,
we'll need you, Ayanokoji-kun.

121
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:53,090
I understand your proposal.

122
00:07:53,570 --> 00:07:55,280
You'll work with us, then?!

123
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:58,430
I appreciate the offer,

124
00:07:58,870 --> 00:08:01,620
but I can't agree at this stage.

125
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:03,090
How come?!

126
00:08:03,090 --> 00:08:06,590
I think we need to offer
better conditions.

127
00:08:06,590 --> 00:08:10,910
Besides, to place at the top
of the island survival game,

128
00:08:10,910 --> 00:08:15,830
the best group would be Ryuen-kun,
Kaneda-kun, and Ayanokoji-kun together.

129
00:08:15,830 --> 00:08:19,000
We need to get Ryuen-kun involved.

130
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,970
There's no way!

131
00:08:20,970 --> 00:08:24,600
You really think Ryuen-san
would agree to my plan?

132
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:27,240
I doubt he'd be enthusiastic, no.

133
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:32,610
For now, let's be satisfied
that we were able to convey

134
00:08:32,610 --> 00:08:35,240
our idea to Ayanokoji-kun.

135
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:37,380
Fine, I get it.

136
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:39,990
I don't know if I can
meet your expectations,

137
00:08:40,300 --> 00:08:42,750
but I'll give it some thought.

138
00:08:43,770 --> 00:08:45,250
Hey, Shinohara!

139
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:46,690
What do you want?

140
00:08:46,690 --> 00:08:48,780
Um, you know...

141
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:51,580
Have you figured out who
you're partnering with yet?

142
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:54,970
No. Why do you ask?

143
00:08:54,970 --> 00:08:59,000
O-Oh, no reason! Just figured I'd ask!

144
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,220
Oh, really?

145
00:09:00,220 --> 00:09:03,530
You'll be with Sudo-kun and
Hondo-kun regardless, right?

146
00:09:03,860 --> 00:09:05,400
What's wrong with that?!

147
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:08,720
I'll have more fun with those guys anyway!

148
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,150
Yes, I'm sure.

149
00:09:10,490 --> 00:09:14,810
But while I'm sure those guys
could figure it out without me...

150
00:09:14,810 --> 00:09:20,530
I'd be happy to lend you a
hand if you needed it, so...

151
00:09:20,950 --> 00:09:23,810
If you need some help, y'know...

152
00:09:23,810 --> 00:09:26,920
I'd be willing to group
up with you, y'know?

153
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:28,170
What's this all about?

154
00:09:28,170 --> 00:09:31,170
You want to be in a group with me?

155
00:09:31,170 --> 00:09:34,080
D-Don't get the wrong idea, okay?!

156
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:37,800
Look, you could actually get
expelled over this, right?!

157
00:09:38,290 --> 00:09:40,020
So, as an expression of my kindness,

158
00:09:40,020 --> 00:09:43,340
I'm willing to take the
hit and keep you safe!

159
00:09:44,070 --> 00:09:47,380
What do you mean, "take the hit"?

160
00:09:47,380 --> 00:09:48,810
I never asked you.

161
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:51,940
Good morning, Ike-kun!

162
00:09:52,170 --> 00:09:53,730
Do you have a minute?

163
00:09:53,730 --> 00:09:56,570
Yeah, I've got nothing better
to be doing right now!

164
00:09:56,570 --> 00:10:01,780
Kobashi-san from Class C wants
to invite you to join her group.

165
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:04,200
Would you be willing
to discuss it with her?

166
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:07,080
You mean it?! Heck yeah,
I'm on my way right now!

167
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:11,710
But you were talking to Shinohara-san
just now, weren't you?

168
00:10:11,970 --> 00:10:13,460
You really want to go?

169
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:15,050
It's fine by me.

170
00:10:15,050 --> 00:10:17,910
He wouldn't stop blabbing at me,
and it was so annoying.

171
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:19,340
Take him wherever you want.

172
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:22,840
I'm the one who's annoyed right now!

173
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:24,510
C'mon, let's go!

174
00:10:25,270 --> 00:10:28,360
I guess someone else needs me, huh?!

175
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,490
Satsuki.

176
00:10:33,970 --> 00:10:35,510
Komiya-kun...

177
00:10:37,110 --> 00:10:38,440
Ayanokoji-kun.

178
00:10:39,030 --> 00:10:40,950
You're in deep trouble.

179
00:10:40,950 --> 00:10:43,530
You actually drew the "Trial" card.

180
00:10:43,530 --> 00:10:45,600
Eight types of cards
with special effects,

181
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:48,410
distributed to students for the test...

182
00:10:48,410 --> 00:10:55,920
Trial:
You may increase your class points
awarded in the special test by 50%.
However, if not in the top 30% of groups,
your group will receive a penalty.
The extra points will be provided by the school.

183
00:10:48,410 --> 00:10:52,600
In exchange for increasing our
class points earned by 50%,

184
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:55,940
you'll suffer a penalty if you
don't place in the top 30%.

185
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:59,230
I doubt anyone would trade for that card.

186
00:10:59,590 --> 00:11:03,930
It looks like you'll have no choice
but to aim for a high placement.

187
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:08,810
I'm afraid I could also get rid of it
if I find someone who wants to trade.

188
00:11:08,810 --> 00:11:11,830
It's up to you which you choose.

189
00:11:11,830 --> 00:11:14,450
I just hope you can find someone
who wants it in the first place.

190
00:11:15,990 --> 00:11:19,530
And just so you know,
I was being sarcastic.

191
00:11:19,530 --> 00:11:20,850
I'll bet.

192
00:11:20,850 --> 00:11:24,830
Punishment for what you
put me through every day.

193
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:27,850
I'm not trying to
"put you through" anything.

194
00:11:27,850 --> 00:11:29,700
Hey, you—

195
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:32,500
You found a partner?!

196
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:34,540
Yeah. That a problem?

197
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:37,800
But I invited you just the other day!

198
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:41,800
And we're not supposed to partner
up until Horikita says so!

199
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:45,730
I don't need permission
for a handshake agreement.

200
00:11:45,730 --> 00:11:48,600
Though I fully intend to
make it official today.

201
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:52,810
Who did you partner up with?!

202
00:11:52,810 --> 00:11:54,740
Komiya-kun from Class B.

203
00:11:54,740 --> 00:11:56,440
What?! Komiya?!

204
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:59,440
That playboy from the basketball team?!

205
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:01,320
He's not a playboy.

206
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:04,200
We're going to discuss it
at the café after class.

207
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,750
I'm so glad you're willing
to partner with me.

208
00:12:10,750 --> 00:12:12,710
Thanks for asking!

209
00:12:13,690 --> 00:12:14,830
What's the status?

210
00:12:14,830 --> 00:12:17,710
It doesn't seem like the
worst case possible,

211
00:12:18,250 --> 00:12:20,140
but he seems really depressed about it.

212
00:12:20,710 --> 00:12:22,530
I'd like to avoid a situation

213
00:12:22,530 --> 00:12:25,710
where Ike can't meet his
potential due to Shinohara.

214
00:12:26,060 --> 00:12:27,470
What should we do?

215
00:12:27,470 --> 00:12:31,100
He doesn't seem about to go off the rails,

216
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,980
so we can probably wait and watch for now.

217
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:36,230
Yeah.

218
00:12:36,740 --> 00:12:42,270
I'd like to look more into Komiya's
motives for inviting Shinohara.

219
00:12:42,270 --> 00:12:47,540
I'll think up who Ike-kun
can partner with instead.

220
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:48,740
Please do.

221
00:12:54,210 --> 00:12:55,870
You don't seem too surprised.

222
00:12:55,870 --> 00:12:58,900
Did you realize I was following you?

223
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:01,380
I just tend not to show my surprise.

224
00:13:01,650 --> 00:13:04,380
What were you talking to Hirata-kun about?

225
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:07,730
Ike-kun? Because of the island test?

226
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:11,010
Is that any of your business?

227
00:13:11,010 --> 00:13:12,680
Don't put up those defenses.

228
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:17,050
There's just something I figured I
should tell you ASAP, so I reached out.

229
00:13:17,050 --> 00:13:18,770
What's that?

230
00:13:18,770 --> 00:13:22,230
The Trial card is a tough one, huh?

231
00:13:22,230 --> 00:13:26,400
If you have any trouble,
I'd be happy to help you out.

232
00:13:26,710 --> 00:13:29,020
You think that the two of us

233
00:13:29,020 --> 00:13:32,510
working together would give the
greatest chance of survival?

234
00:13:33,060 --> 00:13:33,910
You could tell?

235
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:38,920
I thought if I didn't hurry,
you might get sold out.

236
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:43,440
I won't form my group until
the month is out, at least.

237
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:46,010
I'd like to see what other
classes are up to first.

238
00:13:46,010 --> 00:13:50,090
Got it. So there's nothing
I can say at the moment.

239
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:52,390
Think about it, though.

240
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:55,640
Here. My personal contact info.

241
00:13:57,060 --> 00:13:58,230
See ya!

242
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:02,150
Hey!

243
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:05,150
You ready to join us?

244
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:07,740
Sorry, but this is about something else.

245
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:10,490
You want my advice, then?

246
00:14:10,490 --> 00:14:14,510
So you ran off to meet
with Ayanokoji-kun, huh?

247
00:14:14,510 --> 00:14:17,630
Hey, Nishino! I told you not to tag along!

248
00:14:17,630 --> 00:14:21,630
You two are close, huh? Weird pairing.

249
00:14:21,860 --> 00:14:24,450
You aren't listening!

250
00:14:24,450 --> 00:14:26,260
This is why no one likes you!

251
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:29,240
I've got everything I need.

252
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:33,260
And I'm curious as to why
you're meeting up in secret.

253
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:37,400
I wanted his advice about Komiya.

254
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:38,520
Komiya-kun?

255
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:42,620
I heard he wants to group up
with Shinohara from our class.

256
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:46,280
I want to know what kind of person he is.

257
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:48,780
He's just a good guy, y'know?

258
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:50,280
Athletic, too!

259
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,660
Are they going out?

260
00:14:53,910 --> 00:14:56,270
I-I dunno how to answer that...

261
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:59,050
Ishizaki's the last person
to ask about romance.

262
00:14:59,050 --> 00:15:01,040
And you're not?!

263
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:03,660
I'm better than you, at least.

264
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:09,880
They're not dating, but Komiya-kun has
a crush on Shinohara-san for sure.

265
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:11,890
What? For real?

266
00:15:12,940 --> 00:15:16,770
I guess he did mention liking
a girl in another class...

267
00:15:17,210 --> 00:15:20,130
But why are you worried about that?

268
00:15:20,130 --> 00:15:24,380
Ike in our class has a crush on Shinohara.

269
00:15:24,380 --> 00:15:25,450
Huh?

270
00:15:25,450 --> 00:15:29,280
You really shouldn't get involved
in other people's love lives.

271
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:31,460
Normally, I wouldn't.

272
00:15:31,460 --> 00:15:34,490
But I can't ignore it when
it concerns my class.

273
00:15:34,490 --> 00:15:38,510
We need Ike at his best, after all.

274
00:15:38,510 --> 00:15:40,960
Okay! I'll lend you a hand!

275
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:43,180
Ishizaki, are you serious?

276
00:15:43,180 --> 00:15:44,960
You're, like, Komiya's best friend.

277
00:15:45,290 --> 00:15:49,400
Still, I can't ignore Ayanokoji
when he needs help!

278
00:15:49,750 --> 00:15:51,760
So, what should I do?

279
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:53,650
Let's see...

280
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:59,640
Komiya wants to tell Shinohara how
he feels while they're on the island.

281
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:01,460
Why not let him, then?

282
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:07,390
I was wondering what you
wanted to talk to me about...

283
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:10,530
but I don't see why this
is anyone's business.

284
00:16:10,530 --> 00:16:12,050
I'm not sure.

285
00:16:12,530 --> 00:16:17,780
Ike might slip up if he's distracted
by the Shinohara business.

286
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:21,540
You think he could end up
expelled due to heartbreak?

287
00:16:21,910 --> 00:16:25,210
I can't say it's not a possibility.

288
00:16:25,210 --> 00:16:28,170
That would be extremely foolish.

289
00:16:28,170 --> 00:16:31,030
What if Ike-kun tells
her how he feels first?

290
00:16:31,030 --> 00:16:34,050
Get the slate clear so
he can focus on the test.

291
00:16:34,050 --> 00:16:35,800
Does it work like that?

292
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:38,880
Despite all the fields in which you excel,

293
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:41,910
you seem utterly hopeless
when it comes to love.

294
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:44,440
I'm learning a lot.

295
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:45,770
Very well.

296
00:16:45,770 --> 00:16:50,800
You want me to guide Ike-kun and
Shinohara-san to end up together?

297
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:51,580
Yeah.

298
00:16:56,250 --> 00:16:59,710
I'm afraid it might already be too late.

299
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:06,100
Advanced Nurturing High School Administration
Announcement of Island Survival Game
Group Formation
Class 2-B  Komiya Kyogo
Class 2-B  Kinoshita Minori
Class 2-D  Shinohara Satsuki
The listed members have formed a small group.

300
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:11,060
You're not going to pair
with anyone? How come?

301
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:13,920
Being by myself will
make me more flexible.

302
00:17:14,430 --> 00:17:19,930
And taking first place by myself
will gain us 300 class points.

303
00:17:19,930 --> 00:17:24,180
You seem so confident, I feel
like you might just do it...

304
00:17:24,870 --> 00:17:28,380
If you take solo first place,
I might pass out from happiness!

305
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:30,590
You'd be so awesome!

306
00:17:31,770 --> 00:17:38,070
I wish you'd partner with me...
and protect me, though.

307
00:17:38,350 --> 00:17:41,540
There's a way to save you regardless.

308
00:17:42,220 --> 00:17:46,130
Get enough private points to save you.

309
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,330
Well, sure, that's a possibility...

310
00:17:48,550 --> 00:17:50,530
But even in a six-person group,

311
00:17:50,530 --> 00:17:54,670
each person would need a million
points to prevent expulsion, right?

312
00:17:54,670 --> 00:17:56,860
I don't have that much.

313
00:17:57,190 --> 00:17:58,740
How many do you have now?

314
00:17:58,740 --> 00:18:02,040
Um... 240,000 points.

315
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:05,600
I've been saving up pretty well lately!

316
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:08,540
760,000 to make up, then.

317
00:18:09,810 --> 00:18:15,030
Even if I gave her my entire stock
of 250,000, she'd be 500,000 short.

318
00:18:16,060 --> 00:18:16,850
Kei.

319
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:19,240
I'll get you the money.

320
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:23,130
S-Sure. Thanks.

321
00:18:24,370 --> 00:18:29,050
The special test to have me expelled
lasts until the start of the second term.

322
00:18:29,530 --> 00:18:34,510
The next test might be the final
battle for Tsukishiro and me.

323
00:18:34,990 --> 00:18:38,330
If I grouped up with her and
got her involved in my baggage,

324
00:18:38,330 --> 00:18:40,510
the consequences would be severe.

325
00:18:41,190 --> 00:18:44,740
So, what did you want to talk to me about?

326
00:18:44,740 --> 00:18:46,780
I'll be blunt.

327
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:50,400
At the rate you're going,
your class is unlikely

328
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:53,650
to return to Class B,
let alone reach Class A.

329
00:18:55,090 --> 00:18:57,280
That is pretty blunt.

330
00:18:57,560 --> 00:19:00,380
Unfortunately, that's not all.

331
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:06,540
It seems to me that it's only a matter
of time until you fall to Class D.

332
00:19:07,010 --> 00:19:10,650
I understand why you feel that way.

333
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:11,570
But—

334
00:19:11,570 --> 00:19:14,290
You're about to say
something abstract like,

335
00:19:14,290 --> 00:19:16,960
"We'll fight our way through with
effort and friendship," right?

336
00:19:18,040 --> 00:19:21,160
You won't be able to win like that.

337
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:24,550
I've seen no growth in
your class as a whole.

338
00:19:24,550 --> 00:19:25,960
That's...

339
00:19:26,310 --> 00:19:27,810
That's not true!

340
00:19:28,070 --> 00:19:30,620
Everyone's definitely growing!

341
00:19:30,620 --> 00:19:33,310
It's clear as day from your OAA.

342
00:19:33,670 --> 00:19:38,700
Your class has unquestionably had the
slowest growth out of the four classes.

343
00:19:40,090 --> 00:19:44,180
You've proven unable to show your full
potential in unfavorable circumstances.

344
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:45,880
People like Ryuen-kun and me

345
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:48,420
are able to bare our fangs even
when the odds are against us.

346
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:52,330
You stand no chance of
victory as you are now.

347
00:19:52,330 --> 00:19:55,210
I think that's an uncontroversial
statement at this point.

348
00:19:56,030 --> 00:19:59,710
You called me here to say that?

349
00:19:59,710 --> 00:20:04,220
If I merely meant to chastise you,
I wouldn't waste both our time.

350
00:20:05,090 --> 00:20:08,470
Will you work with me, Ichinose-san?

351
00:20:09,730 --> 00:20:14,280
It's the only way you can
catch up with Class A.

352
00:20:14,850 --> 00:20:19,110
I can't imagine what you'd get
out of a partnership with us.

353
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:24,150
True. You have little to offer us
in terms of competitive potential.

354
00:20:24,150 --> 00:20:27,830
But you have a powerful weapon
that no other class has.

355
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:31,010
Trust, of course.

356
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:34,090
I am confident that you will not
betray me under any circumstances.

357
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:38,090
That is a crucial element
when taking a partner.

358
00:20:38,510 --> 00:20:43,780
You may not be able to catch up to us,
but you can overtake Ryuen-kun's class

359
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:46,840
and put more distance
between you and Class D.

360
00:20:47,220 --> 00:20:51,100
Shouldn't your priority right
now be to achieve stability?

361
00:20:51,430 --> 00:20:53,100
Sakayanagi-san...

362
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:56,030
may I be honest with my opinion?

363
00:20:56,030 --> 00:20:57,360
Of course.

364
00:20:57,360 --> 00:21:02,360
I think you're just afraid of the other
three classes teaming up against you.

365
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:05,860
We could certainly sabotage
you if we all worked together.

366
00:21:06,190 --> 00:21:08,550
If such an attempt were to succeed,

367
00:21:08,550 --> 00:21:11,830
it would put you in a very
bad spot moving forward.

368
00:21:12,310 --> 00:21:13,790
Am I wrong?

369
00:21:18,290 --> 00:21:23,210
It seems I may have underestimated you.

370
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:26,360
If you agree to work with me,

371
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:30,100
I am willing to give you enough points
to prevent three people's expulsion.

372
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:32,920
As I know you do not wish
to see anyone expelled,

373
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:34,820
I'm sure you'll find
this a tempting offer.

374
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:37,100
What about five people's worth?

375
00:21:37,370 --> 00:21:40,360
That would certainly let me rest easy.

376
00:21:40,870 --> 00:21:42,890
How very greedy of you.

377
00:21:43,540 --> 00:21:47,020
I expect to receive an amount
similar to that very soon,

378
00:21:47,020 --> 00:21:49,370
so I'll make the payment just for you.

379
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:52,870
You have a deal.

380
00:21:54,870 --> 00:21:58,500
Ryuen-kun and Horikita-san
are both fearsome opponents.

381
00:21:58,500 --> 00:22:01,070
We're the ones who will take first place.

382
00:22:01,410 --> 00:22:05,090
I'll do whatever it takes
to make that happen.
